Code Generation for Expression Trees
RegisterHandle genExpr( node ) {
RegisterHandle result, t1, t2;
switch( type of node ) {
case NUM: result = new_name();
emit( loadI, node.val, =>, res );
break;
case ID: t1 = base( node.val );
t2 = offset( node.val );
result = new_name();
emit( loadAO, t1, t2, =>, res );
break;
case PLUS: t1 = genExpr( node.left_child );
t2 = genExpr( node.right_child );
result = new_reg_name();
emit( add, t1, t2, =>, res );
break;
}
return result;
}
RegisterHandle is a simple integer, we
can refer to the register by this identifier
We define some temporary variables to
store register handles.
We next do an operation for the
appropriate type of expression AST node
(number, variable, addition)

